    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0519" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg423"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Draper.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 344.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 301, of the 11th of
                    October last, I inclose for your information copy of the Department’s No. 29, of
                    the 15th ultimo, to our consul-general at Rome directing the system of consular
                    inspection of emigrants, instituted at Naples, to be carried on without charge,
                    save for actual expenses incurred, and to be extended to Genoa and other Italian
                    ports.</p>
                <p>I am, etc,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d361-a1.xml" xpointer="d361-a1"/>
